Re: soccer, telephone boothes, robocop..
 
Hey, what's the history of these dungeons, anyway?  Did they form from the dust
of the cosmos, randomely? Were they hand assembled by armies of quivering
slaves bowing before the lashes of an evil type character? WHo built it, and
why did they install a soccer stadium?
 
One answer which works for me, but isn't all THAT permissive is that some
ancient thing built the dungeon, and since that time various tribes and groups
of humans have entered it, kindof like mice into a handy hole in th' earth.
Anyway, and then they have developed their own existence inside the dungeon,
some set up shops to deal with the othr humans, some become theifs, some explore
deeper (or higher, depending on the dungeon) and come closer to the source of
that ancient great power and presumably become evil nasti people.
  Hence, it seems that new versions of Hack could have more NPC (non player
character) dynamics. ie. OTHER adventurers besides yourself, other people buying
stuff from shops, sometimes antagonism and sometimes cooperation beteen npc's and npc's as well as npc's and you..   Families, etc..
